[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2800190674","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105367#issuecomment-2800190674","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105367","id":2800190674,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6m54TS","user":{"login":"mdkdir","id":42262007,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMjYyMDA3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42262007?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir","html_url":"https://github.com/mdkdir","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-13T23:58:22Z","updated_at":"2025-04-14T01:12:10Z","body":"> You are right that `CowData` already does the same check, but at this point in the function hierarchy, information about negative indices is lost (since `CowData` doesn't deal with them — `Array` does). \r\n\r\nThe incorrect check already has this behavior. The error only contains the index after the calculation is done.\r\n\r\n```c++\r\nif (p_pos < 0) {\r\n    // Relative offset from the end.\r\n    p_pos = _p->array.size() + p_pos;\r\n}\r\n\r\nERR_FAIL_INDEX_V_MSG(p_pos, _p->array.size(), ERR_INVALID_PARAMETER, vformat(\"The calculated index %d is out of bounds (the array has %d elements). Leaving the array untouched.\", p_pos, _p->array.size()));\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe \"calculated index\" it mentions being p_pos after it's already been added to the size.\r\nThe other pull request you mentioned (#105334) does not change this behavior.\r\n\r\nHere's an example of what it looks like now (with the broken check):\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar array := [0, 1]\r\narray.insert(2, 2) # The calculated index 2 is out of bounds (the array has 2 elements). Leaving the array untouched.\r\narray.insert(-5, -5) # The calculated index -3 is out of bounds (the array has 2 elements). Leaving the array untouched.\r\narray.insert(-1, -1) # <OK>\r\narray.insert(52, 52) # The calculated index 52 is out of bounds (the array has 3 elements). Leaving the array untouched.\r\n```\r\n\r\nWith either fix, `array.insert(2,2)` would not give an error, but other than that, the output would be about the same. Here's what it looks like with my pull request:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar array := [0, 1]\r\narray.insert(2, 2) # <OK>\r\narray.insert(-5, -5) # Index p_pos = -2 is out of bounds (new_size = 4).\r\narray.insert(-1, -1) # <OK>\r\narray.insert(52, 52) # Index p_pos = 52 is out of bounds (new_size = 5).\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhich seems better to me since it's also using the new size for its numbers.\r\nIn any case, there is no instance where the original index is displayed in the error.\r\n\r\n> So the error message would complain that \"index 3 is out of bounds\" when you actually passed index `-2`.\r\n\r\nA negative index will never display an out of bounds error with a positive number, since adding array.size() and a negative number will always be less than array.size(), so at the very least, the error message will contain a negative number if it is out of bounds.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2800190674/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2800995615","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105367#issuecomment-2800995615","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105367","id":2800995615,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6m880f","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-14T09:10:42Z","updated_at":"2025-04-14T09:54:17Z","body":"> > You are right that `CowData` already does the same check, but at this point in the function hierarchy, information about negative indices is lost (since `CowData` doesn't deal with them — `Array` does). \n> \n> \n> \n> The incorrect check already has this behavior. The error only contains the index after the calculation is done.\n\nYou're right. I think it would be good to change the error message for this reason, and print the given index instead of the calculated one. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2800995615/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2802639980","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105367#issuecomment-2802639980","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105367","id":2802639980,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nDORs","user":{"login":"mdkdir","id":42262007,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMjYyMDA3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42262007?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir","html_url":"https://github.com/mdkdir","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-14T18:46:15Z","updated_at":"2025-04-14T18:46:15Z","body":"> I think it would be good to change the error message for this reason, and print the given index instead of the calculated one.\r\n\r\nIt was never my goal to add such a feature, and I consider that to be outside the scope of this patch. I only wanted to fix this very important issue. I wanted nothing to do with negative indices or the error message they provide.\r\n\r\nIf you think that feature is a good idea, you may make another commit. Change it when it needs to be changed, not when it needs fixing.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2802639980/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hoora